  "success": true,
  "output": "I reviewed the whole app (Next.js 16 / React 19 — no database, so \"N+1\" shows up as repeated client-side lookups/fetches rather than SQL). Found 31 action entries, ~90 project files, a small `useSyncExternalStore`-based global store, and a couple of WebGL/canvas components. Here's what I found, grounded in actual files/lines.\n\n## 1. N+1-style / repeated-lookup patterns\n\n**`features/actions/ActionLibrary.js:103`** — `ACTIONS.indexOf(action)` is called inside `.map()`, turning an O(n) render into O(n²):\n\n```js\n// now\n{visible.map((action) => (\n  <ActionCard key={action.id} action={action} index={ACTIONS.indexOf(action)} />\n))}\n\n// fix — use the map index directly, it's already stable\n{visible.map((action, i) => (\n  <ActionCard key={action.id} action={action} index={i} />\n))}\n```\n\n**`ActionLibrary.js:31` and `ActionFinder.js:134`** — `ACTION_CATEGORIES.find((c) => c.id === action.category)` runs once *per card, per render*, scanning the categories array every time:\n\n```js\n// add once at module scope in both files\nconst CATEGORY_BY_ID = new Map(ACTION_CATEGORIES.map((c) => [c.id, c]));\n// then: CATEGORY_BY_ID.get(action.category)\n```\n\n**`app/api/air-quality/route.js`** — not currently called from any client component (I grepped — no references outside the route file itself and `config/dataSources.js`). Not a bug today, but if a multi-city view gets added, fetch all cities with `Promise.all`, not a sequential loop — the route already does the hard part right (`next: { revalidate: 900 }`, 8s timeout).\n\n## 2. Unnecessary React re-renders\n\n**The big one — `features/progress/store.js` + every consumer of `useHavoState()`.** The store returns the *entire* top-level state object with no selector:\n\n```js\n// store.js:106\nexport function useHavoState() {\n  return useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, getSnapshot, getServerSnapshot);\n}\n```\n\n`dispatch()` creates a new top-level object on **any** action — toggling a checklist item, recording a quiz score, adding a proposal. Since `AddToPlanButton.js:14` and `Header.js:19` both call `useHavoState()` directly, every one of the ~31 `<AddToPlanButton>` instances across the page (in `ActionLibrary`, `ActionFinder`, planner) **and** the header re-render whenever *any* unrelated slice of state changes.\n\n```js\n// features/planner/AddToPlanButton.js:14\nconst state = useHavoState();          // re-renders on ANY store change\nconst added = isInPlan(state, item.kind, item.refId);\n\n// components/layout/Header.js:19\nconst { plan } = useHavoState();       // same problem\n```\n\nFix: use `useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector` (from `use-sync-external-store/with-selector`, or `react`'s own export path) so components only re-render when their slice changes:\n\n```js\nimport { useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector } from 'use-sync-external-store/with-selector';\n\nexport function useHavoSelector(selector, isEqual) {\n  return useSyncExternalStoreWithSelector(subscribe, getSnapshot, getServerSnapshot, selector, isEqual);\n}\n// AddToPlanButton: useHavoSelector(s => isInPlan(s, item.kind, item.refId))\n// Header: useHavoSelector(s => s.plan.filter(p => !p.completedAt).length)\n```\n\n**`features/actions/ActionFinder.js:124`** — the list key includes `JSON.stringify(submitted)`:\n\n```js\n<motion.li key={`${action.id}-${JSON.stringify(submitted)}`} ...>\n```\n\nThis computes `JSON.stringify` for every item on every render *and* gives every item a brand-new key on each search, so React/Framer Motion unmount+remount the entire list instead of diffing it — defeating `AnimatePresence`'s exit transitions and forcing full re-creation of DOM nodes. Fix: `key={action.id}`.\n\n**`ActionFinder.js:29`** — ranking is recomputed on every render, not just when `submitted` changes:\n\n```js\nconst results = submitted ? recommendActions(submitted) : null; // recalculated even when only `answers` changed\n\n// fix\nconst results = useMemo(() => (submitted ? recommendActions(submitted) : null), [submitted]);\n```\nEvery radio click updates `answers` and re-renders `ActionFinder`, which re-runs `recommendActions` over all 31 actions even though the committed `submitted` hasn't changed. Contrast this with `features/impact/ImpactCalculator.js:66`, which does this correctly (`useMemo` keyed on `[inputs, carFactor]`) — worth using as the template.\n\n## 3. Caching opportunities\n\n- Apply the `Map`-lookup fix above for `ACTION_CATEGORIES`/`EFFECTS` — turns repeated `.find()` into O(1).\n- `hooks/useMediaQuery.js:17` — `getSnapshot` calls `window.matchMedia(query)` fresh on *every render* (not just on subscribe), allocating a new `MediaQueryList` each time instead of reusing the one already created in `subscribe`:\n```js\n// now: new MediaQueryList every render\n() => window.matchMedia(query).matches\n\n// cache per query string at module scope\nconst mqlCache = new Map();\nfunction getMql(query) {\n  if (!mqlCache.has(query)) mqlCache.set(query, window.matchMedia(query));\n  return mqlCache.get(query);\n}\n// getSnapshot: () => getMql(query).matches\n```\n- `app/api/air-quality/route.js` already does the right thing with `next: { revalidate: 900 }` — good pattern, nothing to change there.\n\n## 4. Memory leaks\n\nMost of the codebase is actually careful here — `useInViewport`, `useActiveSection`, `useDialogBehavior`, `AtmosphereField`, `InversionLab`, and the `storage`/`pointermove` listeners all clean up correctly in effect return functions. One real gap:\n\n**`components/three/HeroScene.js:346-351`** — the WebGL context-lost listener is attached in `onCreated` and never removed:\n\n```js\nonCreated={({ gl }) => {\n  gl.setClearColor(0x000000, 0);\n  gl.domElement.addEventListener('webglcontextlost', (e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    onError?.();\n  });\n  ...\n}}\n```\n`onCreated` fires once per `<Canvas>` mount and this closure captures `onError` from that render — if the prop identity changes later, the listener is stale, and there's no `removeEventListener` paired with it. Low practical impact (the canvas is usually torn down wholesale), but for correctness move it into the existing resource-cleanup effect at `HeroScene.js:212-217`:\n\n```js\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const el = gl?.domElement;\n  const handler = (e) => { e.preventDefault(); onErrorRef.current?.(); };\n  el?.addEventListener('webglcontextlost', handler);\n  return () => el?.removeEventListener('webglcontextlost', handler);\n}, [gl]);\n```\n\n## 5. Redundant computations\n\n- `ActionLibrary.js` `indexOf` + category `.find()` — covered above, the main offenders.\n- `components/layout/Header.js:20` — `plan.filter((p) => !p.completedAt).length` recomputes on every Header render, including ones triggered purely by scroll (`useMotionValueEvent` → `setScrolled`), even though `plan` rarely changes. Wrap in `useMemo`/selector once the store fix above is in place.\n- `components/three/HeroScene.js:137-209` — `resources` (geometries/shaders) are correctly memoized on `[q, quality]` and disposed on cleanup — good pattern, no change needed, just note `q = QUALITY[quality]` so `quality` alone is a sufficient dep (very minor).\n- `features/impact/impact.js` + `ImpactCalculator.js` — this is the best-optimized feature in the app (pure functions, single `useMemo`, no wasted work). Worth using as the internal reference implementation when fixing `ActionFinder`.\n\n**Summary of priority:** the store selector problem (#2) is the one with real, page-wide impact — it fans out through every plan button and the header on unrelated state changes. The `ActionLibrary`/`ActionFinder` lookup and key issues are next, cheap to fix, and visibly break list animations. The WebGL listener leak is low severity. Everything else in the codebase (hooks, canvas cleanup, HTTP caching) is already following good practice.\n",
